\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {R3}{\ignorespaces Comparison of the proposed method (eigenvalue solver) with the approach of Ref.~41 (pre-trained surrogate decoder), with the same data, encoder, posterior model, likelihood and training protocol; one training per approach. The surrogate has the architecture of Ref.~41 and is trained with the natural frequencies and mode shapes of the FE model at the damage states of the training set, until convergence (learning rate halved after 100 epochs without a 1\% improvement of the validation error, and training stopped at $10^{-5}$). Its error is evaluated at 20\,000 damage states drawn uniformly over the admissible domain $[0.45,1]^7$. Performance metrics as defined in R1.3.}}{6}{table.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:surrogate}{{R3}{6}{Comparison of the proposed method (eigenvalue solver) with the approach of Ref.~41 (pre-trained surrogate decoder), with the same data, encoder, posterior model, likelihood and training protocol; one training per approach. The surrogate has the architecture of Ref.~41 and is trained with the natural frequencies and mode shapes of the FE model at the damage states of the training set, until convergence (learning rate halved after 100 epochs without a 1\% improvement of the validation error, and training stopped at $10^{-5}$). Its error is evaluated at 20\,000 damage states drawn uniformly over the admissible domain $[0.45,1]^7$. Performance metrics as defined in R1.3}{table.caption.2}{}}
